*Software:* Twenty-three distinct controls pass across inspector, retained join, and capacity-bridge regression. The actual CLI accepts the hand-specified producer-format r1 fixture, labels a rebased r6 input exact3, and rejects a repeated-value selector. Source hashes, theorem bindings and failed preparation are retained. No production artifact, native build or scientific solver was executed.

*Basis changes:* Full-rank vectors supported below bit k span exactly the k-dimensional low-polynomial space. Invertible input transformations preserve the scoped LFD bounds. FFD2 transfers because literal output rows are reconstructed; output row-span equality alone would not suffice.

*Modular correction:* For formal F=p²+p+s², write F=P Q+R. Actual descent imposes R=0, so former affine chains become L_d=C_d(PQ), generally quadratic in the original coordinates. The no-wrap leading-degree proof cannot discard this correction.

*Exact extension:* Adding quotient bits with F+P Z=0 forces their unique quadratic definitions. For D>=2, original closure embeds into extended closure, and substituting those definitions maps extended cap D into original cap2D. Consequently padded UNSAT refutation degrees differ by at most a factor two, independent of the number of quotient bits. No unrestricted SAT LFD equivalence or growing lower bound is established.

*Evidence:* modular-quotient-transport.md and review; no-wrap-basis-recognition-and-label-transfer.md and review; inspector/retained-join source reviews; bound-join-controls/validation.json. The standalone join is not Rust production integration and preserves whole-case admission as false.
